    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "gpt-4o-mini",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "GPT-4O-MINI"
        },
        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are an expert Technical Recruiter specializing in Software Engineering (SWE). Your job is to rigorously analyze the attached resume against modern engineering standards. Focus heavily on technical stack proficiency, system design/architecture experience, evidence of scale, and business impact (e.g., latency reduction, cost savings, system uptime). Avoid giving high scores for passive participation or buzzword-dense resumes lacking context.\n\nEvaluate the resume across these pillars:\n1. Technical Competency & Execution (languages, frameworks, best practices)\n2. Architecture & Scale (handling distributed systems, data pipelines, infrastructure)\n3. Quantitative Impact (metrics, optimization, delivery)\n\nProvide your evaluation strictly in the following JSON format:\n\n{\n  \"score\": [Integer between 1 and 100],\n  \"classification\": \"[Strong | Average | Weak]\",\n  \"summary\": \"[A concise 3-4 sentence overview of the candidate's career trajectory, core technical identity, and overall fit.]\",\n  \"strengths\": \"- First strength point goes here. - Second strength point goes here. - Third strength point goes here.\",\n  \"concerns\": \"- First concern point goes here. - Second concern point goes here. - Third concern point goes here.\"\n}\n\nCRITICAL OUTPUT FORMATTING RULE: \nThe \"strengths\" and \"concerns\" fields MUST be a single, flat string of plain English text. Do NOT wrap the data inside an array or list format like [\"point1\", \"point2\"]. Do NOT output brackets, trailing quotes, or comma-separated blocks. Output it exactly as a regular paragraph string containing bullet points, identical to how the \"summary\" field is structured.\n\nClassification Guidelines:\n- Strong (85-100): Demonstrates clear ownership of high-impact technical projects, deep mastery of a relevant stack, clear quantitative metrics, and architectural reasoning.\n- Average (60-84): Possesses the required skills and solid execution experience, but projects are standard or metrics are vague/missing.\n- Weak (1-59): Lacks core technical competencies, shows shallow involvement in projects, or relies entirely on listing tools without context.\n\nHere is the resume to evaluate:\n{{ $json.text }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {
          "textFormat": {
            "textOptions": {
              "type": "json_object"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        -1360,
